==English==

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/mɪd/}}
* {{rhymes|en|ɪd|s=1}}
* {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-mid.wav|a=Southern England}}

===Etymology 1===
{{etymon|en|id=middle|:inh|enm:mid<id:middle>|tree=1}}
{{inh+|en|enm|mid}}, {{m|enm|midde}}, from {{inh|en|ang|midd|t=mid, middle, midway}}, from {{inh|en|gmw-pro|*midi}}, from {{inh|en|gem-pro|*midjaz|t=mid, middle|pos=adjective}}, from {{inh|en|ine-pro|*médʰyos|t=between, in the middle, middle}}. 

Cognate with {{cog|nl|midden|t=in the middle}}, {{cog|de|Mitte|t=center, middle, mean}}, {{cog|is|miður|t=middle|pos=adjective}}, {{cog|la|medius|t=middle|pos=noun and adjective}}. See also {{m|en|middle}}. The slang sense may be influenced by terms such as {{m|en|middling}} and {{m|en|midwit}}.

====Adjective====
{{en-adj|-|sup=midmost}}

# {{sid|en|middle position}} Occupying a middle position; [[middle]].
#* {{RQ:Melville Pierre|passage=Passing through the silent village, he heard the clock tell the '''mid''' hour of night.}}
#* {{RQ:en:New York Times|author=Daniel Brown|title=League of Legends Worlds: Can ‘Golden Left Hand’ top ‘Faker’ to earn a grand slam?|url=https://www.nytimes.com/athletic/5044894/2023/11/10/worlds-league-of-legends-lol/|date=2023-11-10|passage=Though teams from China have hoisted the Summoner’s Cup, which goes to the Worlds champion, it’s always been South Korean '''mid''' laners who have starred on those teams. Erzberger said Knight wants to be the first Chinese '''mid''' laner to hoist that trophy — and maybe become a national treasure himself.|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20240608172257/https://www.nytimes.com/athletic/5044894/2023/11/10/worlds-league-of-legends-lol/}}
# {{sid|en|linguistics}} {{lb|en|linguistics}} Made with a somewhat elevated position of some certain part of the tongue, in relation to the palate; midway between the high and the low; said of certain vowel sounds, such as, {{IPAchar|[e o ɛ ɔ]}}.
# {{sid|en|mediocre}} {{lb|en|originally|AAVE|_|and|_|Internet slang}} [[mediocre|Mediocre]]; of [[middling]] quality.
#: {{syn|en|meh|pedestrian|unexceptional|Thesaurus:mediocre}}
#* {{RQ:en:National Public Radio|url=https://www.npr.org/sections/now-playing/2021/07/26/1020734173/lil-nas-x-feat-jack-harlow-industry-baby|passage=The song is one of his best, but its real power comes from the accompanying, highly-stylized video wherein Lil Nas X breaks out of a prison populated with Black gay men (and, for an unspecified reason, Jack Harlow in an unseemly role as the Straight White Savior who delivers a verse that is '''mid''' at best and inappropriate at worst).|title=Lil Nas X, 'INDUSTRY BABY'|date=July 26, 2021|author=Reanna Cruz|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20220527061143/https://www.npr.org/sections/now-playing/2021/07/26/1020734173/lil-nas-x-feat-jack-harlow-industry-baby}}
#* {{RQ:en:New York Times|author=w:James Poniewozik|title=The Comfortable Problem of Mid TV|date=2024-04-27|url=https://www.nytimes.com/2024/04/27/arts/television/mid-tv.html|passage=I’ve watched all of these shows. They’re not bad. They’re simply … '''mid'''. Which is what makes them, frustratingly, as emblematic of the current moment in TV as their stars’ previous shows were of the ambitions of the past.|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20240724192653/https://www.nytimes.com/2024/04/27/arts/television/mid-tv.html}}
#* {{RQ:Guardian|author=Rachel Aroesti|title=In an era of AI slop and mid TV, is it time for cultural snobbery to make a comeback?|date=2025-09-28|url=https://www.theguardian.com/tv-and-radio/2025/sep/28/cultural-snobbery-too-much-studio-rogen-house-of-the-dragon|passage=In an era of AI slop and '''mid''' TV, is it time for cultural snobbery to make a comeback? [title]|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20251008231738/https://www.theguardian.com/tv-and-radio/2025/sep/28/cultural-snobbery-too-much-studio-rogen-house-of-the-dragon}}
#* {{quote-web|en|work=YouTube|url=https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=2U5gI640Uco|date=2026-01-28|title=
They're SO MAD that Gamers Rejected Highguard|passage=...it just seems devoid of passion; it's just so generic, so mid, and in some aspects just bad that it seems like it's a game that just exists to exist... (02:20)}}
# {{sid|en|poor quality}} {{lb|en|internet slang|by extension}} {{U|trashy}}; [[low-quality]].
#: {{syn|en|base|lousy|substandard|Thesaurus:low-quality}}

